I fixed #1186: claude-fable-5-2 is now billed at the vendor's prices instead of Fable 5's. The fix is in commit eb0cddc, and clippy and the full cargo test run both pass.

Sources. Before changing any code I re-fetched both vendor pages and quoted them on #1186:
• Pricing page: Fable 5.2 costs $8 per million input tokens and $40 per million output. A 5-minute cache write is $10, a 1-hour write is $16, and cache hits are $0.20.
• Models overview page: claude-fable-5-2 has a 1M-token context window and a 128K maximum output. yoagent's existing Fable 5 setup already uses those limits, so only the price needed replacing.

The change (src/agent_builder.rs, anthropic_preset): a new entry for claude-fable-5-2 and its dated form (claude-fable-5-2-YYYYMMDD). It reuses Fable 5's setup and swaps in the vendor's prices, and requests still go out with the exact model id the user typed. A comment beside it gives the source URL, the fetch date, and when to remove it: once yoagent ships claude_fable_5_2() (yoagent#456). /cost reads its price from this one place.

Found on the way:
• My first version matched any id starting with claude-fable-5-2. That also caught Fable 5's own dated ids, because claude-fable-5-20260801 starts with those same characters. The existing test every_preset_id_is_priced_by_its_own_constructor failed on it by name. The match now accepts only the exact id or the -YYYYMMDD form, and the dated Fable 5 id is a check in the new test that its price stays unchanged.
• That same existing test also failed when run on its own before my change. Fable 5's prices are only loaded once some other test has triggered loading, so run alone it saw no prices at all. The test now loads them itself.

Evidence:
• New test fable_5_2_bills_the_vendor_page_rates: checks all four price columns exactly for the plain, dated and anthropic/-prefixed ids. It also checks the context window and output setting, and that Fable 5.1, Fable 5 and the dated Fable 5 id keep their old prices.
• Proof the test can fail: I disabled the new entry and the test went red by name, showing the old $10 / $12.50 / $1.00 / $50 prices. After I restored it, the marker count was back to 0 and all 15 tests in the file passed.
• Built binary, before and after: yoyo model info claude-fable-5-2 went from "$10.00 in / $50.00 out" to "$8.00 in / $40.00 out". The other Fable ids are unchanged. Both tables were posted on #1186 before the slow test run, and the commit has the full write-up.

Not changed:
• No yoyo setting can exceed Fable 5.2's 128K output maximum without warning first. That's true for every Fable model and is already tracked in #1148.
• The $16 one-hour cache write isn't modelled, the same as yoagent's Fable 5.1 entry.
• The id isn't on the offered /model list, which matches how claude-fable-5-1 is already handled.

My second comment on #1186 says #1147 covers that list. That was wrong (#1147 is about non-Claude ids), and I posted a correction there.

Docs: cost-tracking.md has a Fable 5.2 row and a line on why it exists. The recorded size of agent_builder.rs in tests/module_size.rs went from 5026 to 5050 lines. The new entry is 13 lines and the rest is earlier growth the record had missed. That gate only prints a warning; I updated the number as the task said.
